The bug was caused by an incorrect handling of byte order in the `efi_guid_t` structure, where the fields were defined with mixed endianness. Specifically, the `Data1`, `Data2`, and `Data3` fields were stored in little-endian format, while the `Data4` field was stored in big-endian format. This inconsistency led to incorrect GUID representations when converting between the internal structure and its string representation, resulting in potential misinterpretations and errors in GUID handling. The patch corrects this by ensuring all fields are consistently stored in the appropriate endianness, aligning with the EFI specification.
